# Vendored Bitnami subcharts are gzip archives. Git's auto-detection happens to
# classify them as binary today, which means `core.autocrlf=true` leaves them
# alone -- but "happens to" is not a guarantee, and this repo is developed on
# Windows where autocrlf is on. A single CRLF substitution inside a .tgz makes
# `helm dependency build` fail with a checksum mismatch against Chart.lock, and
# the error names the checksum, not the line endings, so the cause is not where
# anyone looks first. nivo-backend already lost an afternoon to exactly this
# class of failure with sops-encrypted files.
*.tgz -text
*.gz -text

# Everything Helm reads is text and must land with LF, because the charts are
# rendered inside Linux containers regardless of where they were authored.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.tpl text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
.helmignore text eol=lf
